# Build context for the monorepo root. Three service images (piri, hilt,
# ingot) build with the repo root as context because their go.mod carries a
# `replace => ../<svc>` that Go resolves before it will download anything --
# a context scoped to the service directory fails in `go mod download`.
#
# Each Dockerfile then COPYs only the module directories it needs, so this
# file only has to keep the context transfer small.
.git

# smelt's snapshot archives are 40M of the 53M root context and no Dockerfile
# copies them, so every root-context build (piri, hilt, ingot) was shipping
# them to BuildKit for nothing.
#
# A stricter form -- ignore everything, then allowlist the module directories
# the root-context Dockerfiles COPY -- would trim a few more MB, at the cost
# of a hand-maintained list mirroring those COPY lines. Not worth it for the
# remainder; revisit if the context grows again.
smelt/snapshots
